  "disclosures": [
    "All six verification units (TRAV_A_V1..TRAV_F_V1) ran once on the campaign queue in stage 'verification' and finished with return code 0; no unit failed and no rerun or version bump was needed.",
    "The data-free solver fixture (100 synthetic cases: random, duplicate, scaled-duplicate, duplicate with unequal slack, antiparallel slab, zero-width slab, ball-only, ball+halfspace, zero row, all-zero slack, inactive) ran directly outside the queue, because it touches no person-level array, checkpoint or reader. It imports the campaign two_recipient_adapter.guard.project_slack only as the object under test.",
    "Independence boundary: wires, metrics, the pool NLL/Brier/KL/correct computation and its gradients, task gradients, the projection solver, the finite ladder, the FIT2 24-clause rule and selection, the bootstrap, tie-aware weighted AUC, the envelopes, the Student-t Bonferroni intervals, the group-shuffled null, the control gates and the label rule are all own code in two_recipient_adapter_independent/. The only campaign imports are evaluation_queue.queue_config (queue binding) and, as authorized, task_conditioned_representation.attacks (fit_reader, predict_reader, orientation, orient, attack_split, MODEL_SEED_BASE) and compressed_income_safeguard.readers (tables, kind_for), used for reader refits only.",
    "The own projection solver is mathematically the same KKT active-set principle as the campaign solver: it enumerates halfspace active sets and finds the ball multiplier by bisection, not in closed form, using least-squares affine projections. It is therefore not an algorithmically unrelated method. It was also cross-checked against scipy SLSQP on the synthetic fixtures: own vs campaign max abs 6.9e-18 (100/100 within 1e-12); own vs SLSQP max abs 7.4e-10; own objective never worse than a feasible SLSQP point. Active sets differ in 2/100 degenerate duplicate-row cases, where the solution d is identical.",
    "Counterfactual re-solve: the stage reused the stored pool gradients and the slacks (anchor limits minus the stored pool state), as specified. It independently recomputed and matched pool metrics, pool gradients, task gradients, guard CE gradients and the proposal formula (all differences 0). The contribution tolerance used max(1e-10, 10 x own task-gradient recomputation noise), and since the recomputation noise was 0 it is 1e-10. The probe-wire tolerance is the admitted 1e-10 per block, or any decision change.",
    "Income had no active-budget cases in J_BOTH training (0 saved states in both seeds), so the income solver path was exercised on real data only in its inactive-constraint branch. Active-constraint correctness for that path rests on the data-free fixtures. The occupation real-data states did exercise active KL halfspaces, ball-active states and shortened ladders.",
    "Movement rule: 8/8 first-eight counterfactuals qualify for every recipient-seed. All of them are in epoch 1, phase 1, at or before the nominated J_BOTH E10. Each single displacement is small (privacy-minus-counterfactual max abs about 1.7e-4 to 1.7e-3), but every one is far above the 1e-10 tolerance.",
    "Stage E reads INNER truth through the queue only (allow_inner_truth=True, after the committed REPORTING_LOCK). The coordinator helper coord.unit hashed the INNER truth files while building the unit spec, as the campaign's own report unit did.",
    "The verification_complete input to the label rule was set to 'all other independent checks PASS'. The label is POINT_FEASIBLE_NO_COMPETITIVE_CRITERION whatever that input is, because the primary family has 5 ESTABLISHED_VIOLATION and 21 UNRESOLVED endpoints, including utility endpoints that are not PASS.",
    "Reader refits: 24 of the allowed 36. For seeds 0/1 x {J_BOTH, RAW_PROJ, L_BOTH}, the readers refitted were the pair, r1 and r2 envelope point-max readers on INNER (chosen from Stage E) plus pair LR_C1. All 24 reproduced the frozen INNER_SCORES bitwise, with orientation identical. Own ATT and INNER wire hashes matched the reader receipts.",
    "finalize.py and solver_fixture.py were written or edited after some units had been enqueued. Neither is imported by any unit, and the unit source lists hash every package file that existed at each enqueue."
  ],
